---
const rows: [string, string, string, string][] = [
  ["How art is made", "A diffusion model paints from your prompt", "The agent sets pixels or draws shapes through tool calls", "The agent writes a source file in a text notation that PAGAN compiles"],
  ["Art is stored as", "PNGs", "PNGs or .aseprite files", "Text in git: diffable, reviewable, editable by hand or by agent"],
  ["Cost / access", "Subscriptions or credits, cloud, account", "Free; some need Aseprite (paid)", "Free, MIT, offline"],
  ["Consistent rotations", "4/8 directions generated by a model", "Drawn by hand per direction", "3D voxel models rendered exactly in 1-32 headings with one camera and light"],
  ["Animation consistency", "Model-generated frames", "Manual", "Parts move by whole voxels; lint measures frame-to-frame change; previews highlight every changed pixel"],
  ["Style across a game", "Per prompt / style references", "None", "Project-wide palettes, ramps, camera, light and style versions; change one setting, every asset updates"],
  ["Quality checks", "None", "None", "A linter the agent reads and fixes (orphan pixels, jitter, ramp misuse, outline clipping…)"],
  ["Engine output", "PNG sheets, some JSON atlases", "PNG", "manifest.json for any engine; Godot SpriteFrames / TileSet; normal maps; palette-swap tables"],
  ["Long-term project", "None", "None", "BRIEF.md + STYLE.md memory, asset status, style changelog"],
  ["Deterministic", "No", "Yes", "Yes: byte-identical builds"],
];
---

<section id="compare">
  <div class="wrap">
    <span class="eyebrow">How it compares</span>
    <h2>Three kinds of tool</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Facts as of October 2026, from each tool's own documentation. Pick what fits your game.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col"></th>
            <th scope="col">Image-model generators<small>PixelLab, Ludo, Sprite AI, Retro Diffusion, SpriteLab</small></th>
            <th scope="col">Pixel-pushing MCP servers<small>pixel-mcp, pixscii, Aseprite MCPs</small></th>
            <th scope="col" class="us">PAGAN</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            rows.map(([k, a, b, c]) => (
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">{k}</th>
                <td>{a}</td>
                <td>{b}</td>
                <td class="us">{c}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="where">
      <b>Where PAGAN loses:</b> it isn't a painter. For one-off, organic, illustration-heavy art, a
      diffusion tool is faster. PAGAN wins on a whole game's worth of consistent, animated, rotatable,
      maintainable assets.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    margin-top: 28px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
  }
  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    min-width: 760px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }
  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  thead th {
    font: 0.85rem var(--font-pixel);
    background: var(--panel);
  }
  thead small {
    display: block;
    font: 0.75rem var(--font-body);
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  tbody th {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--muted);
    width: 15%;
  }
  td {
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .us {
    color: var(--text);
    background: rgba(232, 104, 58, 0.07);
  }
  thead .us {
    color: var(--glow);
  }
  tbody tr:last-child > * {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .where {
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 52rem;
  }
  .where b {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
